# Eos runtime state and credentials -- never tracked.
# The root .gitignore re-includes agents/eos/ without a /** glob precisely so
# that this file stays authoritative. .env is the program's de-facto keyring
# (keys.py reads it); it is never read, printed or committed (EOS-04).
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*secret*
*credential*
reports/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pid
state/

# ...but the INSTRUMENTS THAT ENFORCE THE ABOVE ARE SOURCE CODE.
# Found 2026-09-11: the `*credential*` line silently excluded
# src/credential_census.py and tests/test_credential_boundary.py -- the
# census that finds credential leaks and the test that holds the boundary.
# A pattern written to exclude secrets BY NAME also excludes the tooling
# named after them, and git drops it without a word. Same family as the
# Season I bug where the comment documenting a contamination defect
# triggered the defect. Source is re-included explicitly; the credential
# patterns above still bind every non-.py path.
!src/*.py
!tests/*.py
